.page lspci 1 list PCI devices

# SYNOPSIS
*lspci* [*-v*]

# DESCRIPTION
`lspci` shows the PCI devices the kernel found, read from `/proc/pci`. Each line gives the bus address (`bus:device.function`), the class code, the vendor and device ids, the name of the class and, if a driver has claimed the device, the driver's name in brackets.

# OPTIONS
@ *-v*
    Verbose: also print the indented lines that describe each base address register of a device (its kind, address and size).

# EXAMPLES
    lspci
    lspci -v | less

# SEE ALSO
lsusb(1), lsblk(1), dmesg(1)
